,"num_turns":18,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"PKT-0091 is done and committed. Both acceptance commands pass: `sdkjs-word.sh` (42/42 suites, 6195/6195 assertions) and `unit.sh`. `theseus validate` shows 0 errors. I haven't re-measured in the browser yet, so it's still unproven that remote typing now takes the incremental path.\n\n**The change** (`external/sdkjs/word/Editor/CollaborativeEditing.js`): in `private_CollectFontCheckClasses`, changes of type `historyitem_TableId_Description` (131071) are now skipped before the class lookup. Those records carry no fonts. Before this, they put `CTableId` into every remote batch, and that sent every batch down the full walk. The fallback for unknown objects (force the full walk) is unchanged, and the open, save and image paths still use the full walk.\n\n**Surprise:** the packet says to keep PKT-0087's `TableId_Add` branch, but it isn't in this branch's base (sdkjs `theseus` 3d51031). That code (e5fd187) exists only on the fork branch `pkt/PKT-0087`; PKT-0089 applied it for a build and then reverted it. I didn't rewrite it here. Without it, a `TableId_Add` change still falls back to the full walk, which is slower but correct: the font set still covers everything the full walk would collect.\n\n**Decision:** the browser re-measure would change `baseline.md`, which is outside this target. I filed it as a spawn request in `.theseus/spawn/` with `requires: [documentserver, browser]`, including the recipe and the expected result (30/30 batches incremental, about 140 ms saved). `theseus packet new` has no \"measure\" type, so I filed it as `characterize`. Its acceptance only greps `baseline.md` for \"after PKT-0091\", so it can pass even if the 30/30 doesn't happen; the reviewer should check that number.\n\nThe Executor log is filled in and the friction line is appended. No commands were refused.\n\n**Lesson for the Atlas:** every remote Word batch starts with a `CChangesTableIdDescription` record on `CTableId`. Any per-change filter on remote changes has to skip it, or it will see `CTableId` in every batch.","ttft_ms":3263,"type":"result","duration_ms":225736,"uuid":"8a6899f3-63fd-47e6-8463-436e174660e2","ttft_stream_ms":2582,"time_to_request_ms":317,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":4,"system_prompt":200,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":18,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":5,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":6,"engine_pickup":6,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":11,"query_setup":3,"auto_mode_context_wait":13,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":22,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":1,"request_build":7},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":36,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":160,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":214,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":140,"process_rss_mib_result":237,"process_anon_mib_result":143,"process_peak_rss_mib":285,"process_cpu_ms_turn":11944,"process_wall_ms_turn":225735,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":933,"process_wall_ms_streaming":44732,"main_stream_count":18,"main_stream_event_count":898,"main_stream_chunk_count":524,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"artifact_opening_prefetch","slowest_producer_ms":7,"cpu_ms":21,"major_faults":0,"setup_ms":0,"prompt_producers_ms":0,"ambient_start_ms":7,"ambient_wait_ms":6,"render_ms":1,"producers":41,"token_counts":0},"first_content_frame_ms":2582,"time_to_request_from_spawn_ms":9316122,"warm_spare_claimed":false,"flag_fetch_kick":"started_in_init_warm","time_origin_ms":1793668011692.285,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"process_start_tuning":0}
